  "summary": "### Summary",
  "details": "### Summary\r\nA null pointer dereference vulnerability in the Envoy `ext_authz` filter allows an untrusted downstream client to trigger a full process crash (Denial of Service) by sending a path-less CONNECT request when the authorization server is configured to mutate query parameters.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\nWhen the `ext_authz` filter is enabled and receives a successful (`OK`) response from the authorization server that contains query parameter mutations (`query_parameters_to_set` or `query_parameters_to_remove`), it attempts to parse and modify the request's query parameters.\r\n\r\nIn the vulnerable implementation (inside `Filter::onComplete` in [ext_authz.cc](https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/blob/main/source/extensions/filters/http/ext_authz/ext_authz.cc)), the filter attempts to retrieve the path header value using:\r\n```cpp\r\nmodified_query_parameters = Http::Utility::QueryParamsMulti::parseQueryString(\r\n    request_headers_->Path()->value().getStringView());\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, path-less requests (such as standard HTTP/1.1 `CONNECT` requests) do not contain a `:path` header. In this case, `request_headers_->Path()` returns `nullptr`. Calling `->value()` on this null pointer results in a segmentation fault, crashing the entire Envoy worker thread and aborting the proxy process.\r\n\r\n### PoC\r\nTo reproduce the crash:\r\n1. Configure the HTTP Connection Manager (HCM) to accept `CONNECT` requests (e.g., using `upgrade_configs: [{upgrade_type: CONNECT}]` or similar tunnel configurations).\r\n2. Enable the `ext_authz` filter in the HTTP filter chain.\r\n3. Configure the external authorization server to respond with a `CheckResponse` having status `OK` and containing one or more query parameters to set in `query_parameters_to_set` (e.g., `key: \"k\", value: \"v\"`).\r\n4. Send a path-less CONNECT request from a downstream client:\r\n   ```http\r\n   CONNECT host:port HTTP/1.1\r\n   Host: host:port\r\n\r\n   ```\r\n5. On receipt of the authorization server's response, Envoy will immediately crash with a segmentation fault.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n- **Vulnerability Type**: Denial of Service (DoS) via Null Pointer Dereference / Segmentation Fault.\r\n- **Severity**: High (causes immediate full-process termination).\r\n- **Target Audience**: Any deployment using the `ext_authz` filter with query parameter mutations enabled that also routes/proxies path-less `CONNECT` requests.\r\n",
